# Code ownership (audit Z6-15).
#
# There was no CODEOWNERS, so nothing on GitHub distinguished a change to the
# payment ledger from a change to a blog post — every PR looked the same in the
# review queue.
#
# This repo currently has one maintainer, which is exactly why the file is worth
# having rather than a reason to skip it. It does two things today:
#
#  1. it makes the high-consequence paths explicit, so the next contributor (or a
#     future you at 2am) can see at a glance which directories are load-bearing;
#  2. it means adding a second reviewer later is a one-line change per area
#     instead of an archaeology exercise.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so the specific rules below deliberately
# come after the catch-all.

# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                                   @pthirupati

# ── Money. A mistake here is not recoverable by a redeploy. ──────────────────
/backend/apps/billing/              @pthirupati
/backend/apps/certifications/billing_views.py  @pthirupati

# ── Authentication, sessions, MFA, and the permission layer. ────────────────
/backend/apps/accounts/             @pthirupati
/backend/apps/auth_app/             @pthirupati
/backend/common/security.py         @pthirupati
/backend/common/throttles.py        @pthirupati
/backend/common/permissions.py      @pthirupati

# ── Grading. A fail-open grader silently awards credit nobody earned, which is
#    the failure this platform can least afford (see scripts/scan_grader_integrity.py).
/scripts/scan_grader_integrity.py   @pthirupati
/backend/apps/labs/completion.py    @pthirupati
/backend/apps/progress/             @pthirupati

# ── Anything that runs against production. ──────────────────────────────────
/.github/workflows/                 @pthirupati
/deploy/                            @pthirupati
/gateway/                           @pthirupati
/database/                          @pthirupati
/docker-compose*.yml                @pthirupati

# ── Migrations. Reviewed as schema changes, not as code. ────────────────────
/backend/apps/*/migrations/         @pthirupati

# ── Published legal text. Wording here is a commitment, not copy. ───────────
/frontend/src/pages/Privacy.jsx     @pthirupati
/frontend/src/pages/Terms.jsx       @pthirupati
